[1m[35mmarginalia> [0m[0mHere is a summary of goodwill impairment based on the notes:

*   When the fair value of reporting units is less than their carrying value (book value of assets plus goodwill minus liabilities), the goodwill must be reduced to equal the carrying value [S1].
*   Under U.S. GAAP and IFRS, goodwill is generally not amortized for public companies because it is considered to have an indefinite useful life [S2].
*   Private companies may elect to amortize goodwill over ten years or less under an alternative accounting method [S2].
